CYBERSTUDIOS — VISUAL ASSET LICENSE OPT-IN NOTICE

This notice describes how CyberStudios may explicitly designate original
visual assets under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).

CURRENT DESIGNATIONS

No assets are newly designated under CC BY 4.0 by this notice.

Existing artwork licenses and permissions remain unchanged. This file does
not revoke permissions already granted, relicense third-party material, or
automatically place the CyberStudios logo, Cy, Byte, screenshots, or other
artwork under a new license. Its location in assets/ does not determine the
license of files elsewhere in this repository.

HOW AN ASSET IS OPTED IN

A maintainer must make an explicit file-specific designation, either in a
notice accompanying the asset or in a maintained list that identifies its
exact repository path, creator/credit, source, and CC BY 4.0 license.

For example, a future designation may say:
"[exact asset path], created by [creator], is licensed under CC BY 4.0."
That example is a template, not a designation of any existing file.

FOR EXPLICITLY DESIGNATED ASSETS ONLY

The designated original material is offered under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International. The controlling legal terms are available at:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en

License overview:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

CC BY 4.0 permits sharing and adaptation, including commercial reuse, subject
to its terms. Give appropriate credit, retain supplied notices, link to the
license, and indicate changes. Do not imply that CyberStudios endorses your
use. Other applicable rights and third-party licenses may still matter.

When a file has no new designation here, consult its existing notices and
applicable license. The repository's source-code license is in ../LICENSE.
